scope_proof\\\\\\\" has incompatible type \\\\\\\"dict[str, Any] | None\\\\\\\"; expected \\\\\\\"Mapping[str, Any]\\\\\\\"\\\": \\\"scripts/forge/forge_cli/app.py:10047\\\",\\n-  \\\"import-untyped::Skipping analyzing \\\\\\\"forge_cli.engine._engine\\\\\\\": module is installed, but missing library stubs or py.typed marker\\\": \\\"scripts/forge/forge_cli/engine/_command_lock.py:9 (and _finalize.py from wave 4); TYPE_CHECKING-guarded import of a module created in wave 5 \\\\u2014 allowance withdrawn at the wave-5 gate\\\"\\n+  \\\"arg-type::Argument \\\\\\\"scope_request\\\\\\\" to \\\\\\\"_validate_merge_scope_proof\\\\\\\" has incompatible type \\\\\\\"dict[str, Any] | None\\\\\\\"; expected \\\\\\\"Mapping[str, Any]\\\\\\\"\\\": \\\"scripts/forge/forge_cli/app.py:10047\\\"\\n  }\\n }\\n\\\\ No newline at end of file\\ndiff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md\\nindex fb068e1..2d52ca3 100644\\n--- a/CHANGELOG.md\\n+++ b/CHANGELOG.md\\n@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@ Release dates are the UTC dates of the release commits.\\n \\n ### Changed\\n \\n+- Refactor: `scripts/forge/forge_cli/app.py` (11,525 lines) becomes the `forge_cli.app` package — a root `__init__.py` with the verbatim `__all__` and re-exports plus five submodules moved by rope under the AST body oracle (bead forge-plugin-hcuo, plan `.refactor/plan-app.md`): `_mutation_journal.py`, `_admission.py`, `_candidate_observation.py`, `_merge_engine.py` (the `MergeEngine` class, the one new over-budget size-baseline entry at its measured count under the operator ruling on that bead; its class split is a follow-up) and `_dispatch.py`. One non-move edit rides with it: tests patch app-layer controls through one `patch_app` loader helper (E0; the loader sweep rejects raw module patches on app aliases). No body, verb, diagnostic, reason code or `--help` byte changes; the spec's package sentence, the FR-230 production subjects (re-minted), per-module ruff ignores and a `forge_cli.app layers` import-linter contract follow.\\n - Refactor: `scripts/forge/forge_cli/engine.py` (12,178 lines) becomes the `forge_cli.engine` package — a root `__init__.py` with the verbatim `__all__` and re-exports plus 29 submodules moved by rope under the AST body oracle (bead forge-plugin-2fc, plan `.refactor/plan-engine.md`). Two non-move edits ride with it: the merge bootstrap child resolves `scripts/forge/cli.py` from `runtime.py`'s location instead of its own file depth (E1, with a focused test), and tests patch engine controls through one `patch_engine` loader helper (E0; the hermetic chain fixture assigns the codex executable on every engine module that binds it). The reviewer-facing eval trigger table names `scripts/forge/forge_cli/engine/**` in place of `engine.py` in the spec, the policy constant, the rendered project files and the fixtures; the Revision-9 seam-marker loop moves from the `chain_core` package root to `_commit_chain.py` beside `register_coordination_seams` (bead forge-plugin-4j7, finding CON-02; its grandfathered size entry rises 1840 -> 1847 by operator direction of 2026-09-17); the FR-230 production subjects are the engine package files, re-minted; the size baseline is re-pinned at measured sizes (`engine/_engine.py`, the `Engine` class, is the one new over-budget entry), the ruff per-file ignores are narrowed per engine module, and an import-linter layers contract locks the package's wave order.\\n - Test isolation (beads forge-plugin-0eq, forge-plugin-ehn): `tests/test_audit_commitments.py` writes its disabled-control mutants of `audit-commitments.py` under a private temp directory (pinning the script's plugin root) instead of beside the real script, so a parallel Gate 1 shard copying the tracked `scripts/` tree no longer races on a vanishing sibling; `tests/test_mutation_runner.py` sets `FORGE_SESSION_PID` to the test process for the runner child instead of inheriting the caller's value, so an exported session identity no longer fails ten tests with a foreign-live-owner refusal.\\n - chain_core split follow-ups (bead forge-plugin-r0b; review-final findings at reintegration): `scripts/forge/forge_cli/chain_core/_state.py` declares its constants in the historical module order again (bodies unchanged; FR-230 manifest, result fixtures and the v2 byte pin re-minted for the changed production subject); the spec's package sentence names the submodules by the FR-230 manifest's production-subject list instead of the planning document; `pyproject.toml` per-file-ignores drop the dead `chain_core.py` entry and the blanket `chain_core/**` glob in favour of one entry per submodule listing only the codes it trips, and `scripts/check_file_length.py` is cleaned to the full rule set (its entry removed) and gains a focused unittest (`tests/test_check_file_length.py`: hook and plain-mode exit codes, the exact guard diagnostic, and an in-memory control-disable leg); `import-linter==2.15` is pinned beside ruff in the guardrails workflow and the pre-commit setup line. Disclosure: the 0.6.12 reintegration's `.claude/settings.json` also carries `worktree.baseRef: head` and `enabledPlugins: codex-orchestrator@codex-orchestrator` (operator-approved at Gate 4 on 2026-09-14; the plugin entry dangles on a clone without that marketplace). Deferred to the `_commit_chain` split (bead forge-plugin-4j7): moving the Revision-9 seam-marker loop out of the package root, because the grandfathered `_commit_chain.py` may not grow.\\ndiff --git a/docs/specs/forge-plugin-spec.md b/docs/specs/forge-plugin-spec.md\\nindex 59298de..c93ea64 100644\\n--- a/docs/specs/forge-plugin-spec.md\\n+++ b/docs/specs/forge-plugin-spec.md\\n@@ -114,7 +114,7 @@ leaves the commit untouched, records a failed identity verification, and freezes\\n - `agents/review-final.md` — instruction-bounded, execution-capable Claude reviewer with a binding verdict; it has no Edit/Write tools but shares the orchestrator's writable worktree, so its no-write boundary is not an OS sandbox\\n - `scripts/forge/{check-halt.sh,acquire-commit-lock.sh,release-commit-lock.sh,run-evals.sh,invariant-guard.sh,configure-dcg.sh,drift-check.sh,drift-staleness.sh,aggregate-telemetry.sh,commit-guard.sh,install.sh}` and `scripts/forge/{check-test-quality.py,archive-run.py,audit-commitments.py,emit-decision-event.py,journal-patterns.py}` — executable governance script surfaces\\n - `scripts/forge/run-scoped-mutation.py` — Python-interpreter-loaded governance helper (the merge path invokes it as `python3 <path>` and the drift path imports it), so it is outside the executable-script inventory\\n-- `scripts/forge/forge_cli/` — the Python-interpreter-loaded package the Forge CLI is being split into (bead forge-plugin-95e): `scripts/forge/cli.py` remains the sole invoked entry point and shim that FR-221's matcher and the FR-223 corpora pin; the shim puts its own directory on `sys.path`, re-imports the envelope and policy names by explicit named lists, and forwards attribute reads of every `runtime`, `chain_core`, `engine`, and `app` `__all__` export through a module `__getattr__` (PEP 562), so every historical module attribute stays resolvable while tests reach the package through one shared loader (`tests/_cli_loader.py`); no file under it is executable, and it is outside the executable-script inventory exactly as `run-scoped-mutation.py` is. The package holds `envelope.py` (reason codes, `Refusal`, `FrozenError`, `Outcome`), `policy.py` (the committed-policy parser, whose fence helpers are the canonical patch seams), `runtime.py` (the one canonical module for the patchable controls — the clock, the bounded process runner, the merge lifecycle flag, the Revision-9 state controls, the path roots, the lazily imported coordination modules, the fast-tier mechanical-skip predicate, and the late-bound journal-record builder seam — which every module of the split reads by attribute so one in-memory patch on `forge_cli.runtime` disables a control everywhere), `candidate.py` (the shared bounded, pinned Git-context implementation for immutable tree snapshots, deterministic review evidence, marker identity, and raw produced-commit inspection), the `chain_core/` package (`scripts/forge/forge_cli/chain_core/`, whose root `__init__.py` holds the verbatim `__all__` and re-exports every symbol the historical module defined (its unused imports are not re-bound on the root), and whose modules — the root `__init__.py` and the submodules, together exactly the `scripts/forge/forge_cli/chain_core/` production subjects listed in `.forge/evals/tasks/fr230-phase3-4-v2.manifest.json` — hold the fenced process runner, the FR-235 common-lock arbiter and chain leases, chain and merge-chain storage, merge state and transition validation, the ingest verifiers, and the Revision-9 seam-marker loop (in `_commit_chain.py` beside `register_coordination_seams`, with `_seam` re-exported on the root for attribute parity)), the `engine/` package (`scripts/forge/forge_cli/engine/`, whose root `__init__.py` holds the verbatim `__all__` and re-exports every symbol the historical `engine.py` defined (names it merely imported are re-bound on the root only where an importer or test reads them there), and whose submodules — the root and the submodules together exactly the `scripts/forge/forge_cli/engine/` production subjects listed in `.forge/evals/tasks/fr230-phase3-4-v2.manifest.json` — hold the `Engine` commit-chain class (`_engine.py`), argument-parser construction, the finalize pipeline, review transport, approval, secret-scan and fresh-eval helpers, the archive surface, merge admission/scope/claim/epoch/conflict/worktree helpers, and the Revision-12 bootstrap child protocol; `_journal.py` binds the journal-record builder onto the runtime seam at import, and the bootstrap child re-execs `scripts/forge/cli.py` resolved from `runtime.py`'s own location), and `app.py` (`MergeEngine`, the shared chain-verb router, argument-parsing and dispatch entry points, and `main`; it obtains the parser and other engine helpers through `forge_cli.engine`). The existing FR-230 phase-3/4 manifest retains its historical production subjects; every changed or added production subject, including `candidate.py`, requires a current applicable Recorded-baseline integrity (`strict-evals`) result binding, plus `fresh-reviewer-evals` when the authenticated-base trigger matches; an unverifiable trigger blocks through its required INVALID path. The split changes no verb, diagnostic, reason code, `--help` byte, or immutable prior corpus.\\n+- `scripts/forge/forge_cli/` — the Python-interpreter-loaded package the Forge CLI is being split into (bead forge-plugin-95e): `scripts/forge/cli.py` remains the sole invoked entry point and shim that FR-221's matcher and the FR-223 corpora pin; the shim puts its own directory on `sys.path`, re-imports the envelope and policy names by explicit named lists, and forwards attribute reads of every `runtime`, `chain_core`, `engine`, and `app` `__all__` export through a module `__getattr__` (PEP 562), so every historical module attribute stays resolvable while tests reach the package through one shared loader (`tests/_cli_loader.py`); no file under it is executable, and it is outside the executable-script inventory exactly as `run-scoped-mutation.py` is. The package holds `envelope.py` (reason codes, `Refusal`, `FrozenError`, `Outcome`), `policy.py` (the committed-policy parser, whose fence helpers are the canonical patch seams), `runtime.py` (the one canonical module for the patchable controls — the clock, the bounded process runner, the merge lifecycle flag, the Revision-9 state controls, the path roots, the lazily imported coordination modules, the fast-tier mechanical-skip predicate, and the late-bound journal-record builder seam — which every module of the split reads by attribute so one in-memory patch on `forge_cli.runtime` disables a control everywhere), `candidate.py` (the shared bounded, pinned Git-context implementation for immutable tree snapshots, deterministic review evidence, marker identity, and raw produced-commit inspection), the `chain_core/` package (`scripts/forge/forge_cli/chain_core/`, whose root `__init__.py` holds the verbatim `__all__` and re-exports every symbol the historical module defined (its unused imports are not re-bound on the root), and whose modules — the root `__init__.py` and the submodules, together exactly the `scripts/forge/forge_cli/chain_core/` production subjects listed in `.forge/evals/tasks/fr230-phase3-4-v2.manifest.json` — hold the fenced process runner, the FR-235 common-lock arbiter and chain leases, chain and merge-chain storage, merge state and transition validation, the ingest verifiers, and the Revision-9 seam-marker loop (in `_commit_chain.py` beside `register_coordination_seams`, with `_seam` re-exported on the root for attribute parity)), the `engine/` package (`scripts/forge/forge_cli/engine/`, whose root `__init__.py` holds the verbatim `__all__` and re-exports every symbol the historical `engine.py` defined (names it merely imported are re-bound on the root only where an importer or test reads them there), and whose submodules — the root and the submodules together exactly the `scripts/forge/forge_cli/engine/` production subjects listed in `.forge/evals/tasks/fr230-phase3-4-v2.manifest.json` — hold the `Engine` commit-chain class (`_engine.py`), argument-parser construction, the finalize pipeline, review transport, approval, secret-scan and fresh-eval helpers, the archive surface, merge admission/scope/claim/epoch/conflict/worktree helpers, and the Revision-12 bootstrap child protocol; `_journal.py` binds the journal-record builder onto the runtime seam at import, and the bootstrap child re-execs `scripts/forge/cli.py` resolved from `runtime.py`'s own location), and the `app/` package (`scripts/forge/forge_cli/app/`, whose root `__init__.py` holds the verbatim `__all__` and re-exports every symbol the historical `app.py` defined, and whose modules — the root and the submodules together exactly the `scripts/forge/forge_cli/app/` production subjects listed in `.forge/evals/tasks/fr230-phase3-4-v2.manifest.json` — hold the `MergeEngine` merge-chain class (`_merge_engine.py`), merge-start admission (`_admission.py`), current-candidate observation (`_candidate_observation.py`), the deferred mutation-journal sideband helpers (`_mutation_journal.py`), and the shared chain-verb router, the dispatch entry point and `main` (`_dispatch.py`); it obtains the parser and other engine helpers through `forge_cli.engine`). The existing FR-230 phase-3/4 manifest retains its historical production subjects; every changed or added production subject, including `candidate.py`, requires a current applicable Recorded-baseline integrity (`strict-evals`) result binding, plus `fresh-reviewer-evals` when the authenticated-base trigger matches; an unverifiable trigger blocks through its required INVALID path. The split changes no verb, diagnostic, reason code, `--help` byte, or immutable prior corpus.\\n - `scripts/forge/forge_cli/fresh_evals.py` — the non-executable, Python-interpreter-loaded internal collector and verifier for candidate-bound fresh reviewer evaluation; behind the chain-owned `engine/` package launcher adapter it implements authenticated trigger derivation, candidate-tree fixture inventory and oracle withholding, bounded native child execution, canonical request-bound artifacts, manifest verification, and the current-candidate PASS predicate without adding a second CLI entry point\\n - `scripts/forge/cli.py` — the Forge CLI commit-chain slice (FR-210..FR-224): a persisted chain state machine invoked as `python3 \\\"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/forge/cli.py\\\" <verb>`, owning commit-chain sequencing, staging, candidate identity, evidence capture, and finalize. No PATH binary named `forge` is installed (the Foundry `forge` collision); `forge <verb>` anywhere in this spec is shorthand for that invocation form. Phase-gated: ships only after the FR-223 precondition evals pass\\n - Phase-3 Forge CLI merge surfaces specified by FR-230..FR-237: `status`, `merge start|refresh|verify|gate run|approve|finalize|recover|cleanup|abort`, and the shared `review request|attach|disposition` verbs. These are normative future surfaces, not implementation delivered by Revision 7.\\ndiff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml\\nindex e401919..1e6b59d 100644\\n--- a/pyproject.toml\\n+++ b/pyproject.toml\\n@@ -57,7 +57,12 @@ max-nested-blocks = 4\\n \\\"scripts/forge/cli.py\\\" = [\\\"F401\\\", \\\"I001\\\", \\\"UP035\\\"]\\n \\\"scripts/forge/commitment_paths.py\\\" = [\\\"C901\\\", \\\"I001\\\", \\\"PLR0911\\\", \\\"PLR0912\\\"]\\n \\\"scripts/forge/emit-decision-event.py\\\" = [\\\"C901\\\", \\\"I001\\\", \\\"PLR0911\\\", \\\"PLR0912\\\", \\\"PLR0915\\\", \\\"PLR1702\\\"]\\n-\\\"scripts/forge/forge_cli/app.py\\\" = [\\\"B023\\\", \\\"B904\\\", \\\"B905\\\", \\\"C901\\\", \\\"E501\\\", \\\"E731\\\", \\\"F401\\\", \\\"F811\\\", \\\"F841\\\", \\\"I001\\\", \\\"PLR0911\\\", \\\"PLR0912\\\", \\\"PLR0913\\\", \\\"PLR0915\\\", \\\"PLR1702\\\", \\\"UP012\\\", \\\"UP035\\\"]\\n+\\\"scripts/forge/forge_cli/app/__init__.py\\\" = [\\\"I001\\\"]\\n+\\\"scripts/forge/forge_cli/app/_admission.py\\\" = [\\\"C901\\\", \\\"I001\\\", \\\"PLR0912\\\", \\\"PLR0915\\\"]\\n+\\\"scripts/forge/forge_cli/app/_candidate_observation.py\\\" = [\\\"C901\\\", \\\"I001\\\", \\\"PLR0912\\\", \\\"PLR0915\\\", \\\"UP035\\\"]\\n+\\\"scripts/forge/forge_cli/app/_dispatch.py\\\" = [\\\"C901\\\", \\\"E501\\\", \\\"I001\\\", \\\"PLR0911\\\", \\\"PLR0912\\\", \\\"UP035\\\"]\\n+\\\"scripts/forge/forge_cli/app/_merge_engine.py\\\" = [\\\"B023\\\", \\\"B904\\\", \\\"B905\\\", \\\"C901\\\", \\\"E501\\\", \\\"E731\\\", \\\"F841\\\", \\\"I001\\\", \\\"PLR0911\\\", \\\"PLR0912\\\", \\\"PLR0913\\\", \\\"PLR0915\\\", \\\"PLR1702\\\", \\\"UP012\\\", \\\"UP035\\\"]\\n+\\\"scripts/forge/forge_cli/app/_mutation_journal.py\\\" = [\\\"C901\\\", \\\"I001\\\", \\\"UP035\\\"]\\n \\\"scripts/forge/forge_cli/candidate.py\\\" = [\\\"B905\\\", \\\"C901\\\", \\\"E501\\\", \\\"I001\\\", \\\"PLR0911\\\", \\\"PLR0912\\\", \\\"PLR0913\\\", \\\"PLR0915\\\", \\\"PLR1702\\\", \\\"UP035\\\"]\\n # chain_core/ package (split 2026-09-13; narrowed per module 2026-09-14, bead forge-plugin-r0b):\\n # each entry lists only the codes that module trips, so the ratchet can tighten per file.\\n@@ -304,6 +309,23 @@ ignore_imports = [\\n     \\\"forge_cli.runtime -> codex_orchestrator.journal\\\",\\n ]\\n \\n+[[tool.importlinter.contracts]]\\n+# forge_cli.app split (bead forge-plugin-hcuo): wave order of .refactor/plan-app.md; the same\\n+# lazy runtime -> codex_orchestrator cycle as the engine contract is ignored.\\n+name = \\\"forge_cli.app layers\\\"\\n+type = \\\"layers\\\"\\n+containers = [\\\"forge_cli.app\\\"]\\n+layers = [\\n+    \\\"_dispatch\\\",\\n+    \\\"_merge_engine\\\",\\n+    \\\"_admission | _candidate_observation | _mutation_journal\\\",\\n+]\\n+ignore_imports = [\\n+    \\\"forge_cli.runtime -> codex_orchestrator.batch\\\",\\n+    \\\"forge_cli.runtime -> codex_orchestrator.builders\\\",\\n+    \\\"forge_cli.runtime -> codex_orchestrator.journal\\\",\\n+]\\n+\\n # codex_orchestrator must not depend on forge_cli at module import time. The four\\n # function-level imports below are pre-existing lazy cross-links (2026-09-13); they\\n # are ignored here so the contract tracks today's shape. TODO: remove each ignore\\ndiff --git a/tests/_cli_loader.py b/tests/_cli_loader.py\\nindex 01e1234..7622ba3 100644\\n--- a/tests/_cli_loader.py\\n+++ b/tests/_cli_loader.py\\n@@ -92,6 +92,10 @@ def _engine_modules() -> list[ModuleType]:\\n     return _package_modules(\\\"engine\\\")\\n \\n \\n+def _app_modules() -> list[ModuleType]:\\n+    return _package_modules(\\\"app\\\")\\n+\\n+\\n class _PackagePatch:\\n     \\\"\\\"\\\"``mock.patch.object`` applied to every module of ``forge_cli.<package>`` that\\n     binds ``name``, so one test patch keeps intercepting a control after it moves out of\\n@@ -161,3 +165,15 @@ def patch_engine(name: str, /, *args, **kwargs) -> _PackagePatch:\\n     not module patches and stay as ``mock.patch.object``.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n \\n     return _PackagePatch(\\\"engine\\\", name, args, kwargs)\\n+\\n+\\n+def patch_app(name: str, /, *args, **kwargs) -> _PackagePatch:\\n+    \\\"\\\"\\\"Patch ``name`` on the canonical ``forge_cli.app`` module (the package root once\\n+    the application layer is a package) and on every ``forge_cli.app.*`` submodule that\\n+    binds it (see :class:`_PackagePatch`); a context manager with the\\n+    ``mock.patch.object(package_module(\\\"app\\\"), name, ...)`` signature. Use it for every\\n+    module-level patch of an app-layer control so tests are indifferent to which file\\n+    inside the package a control lives in; patches on ``MergeEngine`` (the class) or\\n+    its instances are not module patches and stay as ``mock.patch.object``.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n+\\n+    return _PackagePatch(\\\"app\\\", name, args, kwargs)\\ndiff --git a/tests/test_cli_loader.py b/tests/test_cli_loader.py\\nindex 0c5fe49..b7c9f0b 100644\\n--- a/tests/test_cli_loader.py\\n+++ b/tests/test_cli_loader.py\\n@@ -59,6 +59,16 @@ def _is_engine_module_alias(target: str) -> bool:\\n     return tail == \\\"engine\\\" and bool(prefix) and _is_cli_shaped_alias(prefix)\\n \\n \\n+def _is_app_module_alias(target: str) -> bool:\\n+    \\\"\\\"\\\"Recognize aliases of the canonical ``forge_cli.app`` module (``APP``, ``CLI.app``,\\n+    ``forge_cli.app``) but never the ``MergeEngine`` class nor an instance of it.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n+\\n+    prefix, _, tail = target.rpartition(\\\".\\\")\\n+    if tail == \\\"APP\\\":\\n+        return True\\n+    return tail == \\\"app\\\" and bool(prefix) and _is_cli_shaped_alias(prefix)\\n+\\n+\\n def _literal_string(node: ast.AST) -> str | None:\\n     try:\\n         value = ast.literal_eval(node)\\n@@ -94,8 +104,9 @@ def _write_site(node: ast.Call) -> tuple[str, str, str] | None:\\n \\n def _moved_shim_patch_offenders(path: Path, text: str) -> list[str]:\\n     \\\"\\\"\\\"Find writes whose target is a per-load shim rather than a canonical module, and\\n-    module-level patches on ``forge_cli.engine`` that bypass ``patch_engine`` (a root-only\\n-    patch silently stops intercepting a control once it lives in a package submodule).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n+    module-level patches on ``forge_cli.engine`` or ``forge_cli.app`` that bypass\\n+    ``patch_engine`` / ``patch_app`` (a root-only patch silently stops intercepting a\\n+    control once it lives in a package submodule).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n \\n     offenders: list[str] = []\\n     tree = ast.parse(text, filename=str(path))\\n@@ -115,6 +126,11 @@ def _moved_shim_patch_offenders(path: Path, text: str) -> list[str]:\\n                 f\\\"{path.name}:{node.lineno}: patches engine name {name} on {target}\\\"\\n                 \\\" outside patch_engine\\\"\\n             )\\n+        elif operation == \\\"patches\\\" and _is_app_module_alias(target):\\n+            offenders.append(\\n+                f\\\"{path.name}:{node.lineno}: patches app name {name} on {target}\\\"\\n+                \\\" outside patch_app\\\"\\n+            )\\n     return offenders\\n \\n \\n@@ -255,6 +271,79 @@ mock.patch.object(root, self._name, value)\\n \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n         self.assertEqual(_moved_shim_patch_offenders(Path(\\\"synthetic.py\\\"), accepted), [])\\n \\n+    def test_app_patch_sweep_rejects_raw_module_patches_and_accepts_the_helper(\\n+        self,\\n+    ) -> None:\\n+        \\\"\\\"\\\"Every module-level patch form on forge_cli.app is an offender (app split step\\n+        E0); patch_app, MergeEngine class/instance patches and stdlib attributes are not.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n+        rejected = \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n+mock.patch.object(APP, \\\"dispatch\\\", value)\\n+patch.object(APP, '_merge_command_engine', value)\\n+mock.patch.object(\\n+    APP, \\\"_observe_current_merge_candidate\\\", side_effect=boom\\n+)\\n+mock.patch.object(CLI.app, \\\"dispatch\\\", value)\\n+mock.patch.object(suite.APP, \\\"dispatch\\\", value)\\n+mock.patch(\\\"forge_cli.app.dispatch\\\", value)\\n+patch('forge_cli.app._persist_deferred_mutation_result', value)\\n+\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n+        offenders = _moved_shim_patch_offenders(Path(\\\"synthetic.py\\\"), rejected)\\n+        self.assertEqual(len(offenders), 7)\\n+        self.assertTrue(all(\\\"outside patch_app\\\" in offender for offender in offenders))\\n+        self.assertTrue(any(\\\" on CLI.app \\\" in offender for offender in offenders))\\n+        self.assertTrue(any(\\\" on suite.APP \\\" in offender for offender in offenders))\\n+        self.assertEqual(\\n+            sum(\\\" on forge_cli.app \\\" in offender for offender in offenders), 2\\n+        )\\n+        accepted = \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n+patch_app(\\\"dispatch\\\", value)\\n+with patch_app(\\n+    \\\"_observe_current_merge_candidate\\\", side_effect=boom\\n+):\\n+    pass\\n+mock.patch.object(app, \\\"_halt\\\", value)\\n+mock.patch.object(self.app, \\\"_release_lock\\\", value)\\n+mock.patch.object(APP.os, \\\"environ\\\", value)\\n+mock.patch.object(CLI.MergeEngine, \\\"finalize\\\", value)\\n+mock.patch.object(CLI.MergeEngine, \\\"_recording_common_lock\\\", value)\\n+\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n+        self.assertEqual(_moved_shim_patch_offenders(Path(\\\"synthetic.py\\\"), accepted), [])\\n+\\n+    def test_patch_app_reaches_every_app_module_and_restores(self) -> None:\\n+        \\\"\\\"\\\"patch_app is mock.patch.object on the canonical app root plus every\\n+        forge_cli.app.* submodule binding the name, restoring all of them on exit.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n+        app = _cli_loader.package_module(\\\"app\\\")\\n+        cli = _cli_loader.load_cli(\\\"_cli_loader_test_patch_app\\\")\\n+        modules = _cli_loader._app_modules()\\n+        self.assertIs(modules[0], app)\\n+        for module in modules[1:]:\\n+            self.assertTrue(module.__name__.startswith(\\\"forge_cli.app.\\\"