rt through a module `__getattr__` (PEP 562), so every historical module attribute stays resolvable while tests reach the package through one shared loader (`tests/_cli_loader.py`); no file under it is executable, and it is outside the executable-script inventory exactly as `run-scoped-mutation.py` is. The package holds `envelope.py` (reason codes, `Refusal`, `FrozenError`, `Outcome`), `policy.py` (the committed-policy parser, whose fence helpers are the canonical patch seams), `runtime.py` (the one canonical module for the patchable controls — the clock, the bounded process runner, the merge lifecycle flag, the Revision-9 state controls, the path roots, the lazily imported coordination modules, the fast-tier mechanical-skip predicate, and the late-bound journal-record builder seam — which every module of the split reads by attribute so one in-memory patch on `forge_cli.runtime` disables a control everywhere), `candidate.py` (the shared bounded, pinned Git-context implementation for immutable tree snapshots, deterministic review evidence, marker identity, and raw produced-commit inspection), the `chain_core/` package (`scripts/forge/forge_cli/chain_core/`, whose root `__init__.py` holds the verbatim `__all__` and re-exports every symbol the historical module defined (its unused imports are not re-bound on the root), and whose modules — the root `__init__.py` and the submodules, together exactly the `scripts/forge/forge_cli/chain_core/` production subjects listed in `.forge/evals/tasks/fr230-phase3-4-v2.manifest.json` — hold the fenced process runner, the FR-235 common-lock arbiter and chain leases, chain and merge-chain storage, merge state and transition validation, the ingest verifiers, and the Revision-9 seam-marker loop (in `_commit_chain.py` beside `register_coordination_seams`, with `_seam` re-exported on the root for attribute parity)), the `engine/` package (`scripts/forge/forge_cli/engine/`, whose root `__init__.py` holds the verbatim `__all__` and re-export