mmit-chain slice (FR-210..FR-224): a persisted chain state machine invoked as `python3 \\\"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/forge/cli.py\\\" <verb>`, owning commit-chain sequencing, staging, candidate identity, evidence capture, and finalize. No PATH binary named `forge` is installed (the Foundry `forge` collision); `forge <verb>` anywhere in this spec is shorthand for that invocation form. Phase-gated: ships only after the FR-223 precondition evals pass\\n   120\\t- Phase-3 Forge CLI merge surfaces specified by FR-230..FR-237: `status`, `merge start|refresh|verify|gate run|approve|finalize|recover|cleanup|abort`, and the shared `review request|attach|disposition` verbs. These are normative future surfaces, not implementation delivered by Revision 7.\\n   121\\t- Phase-4 `forge push`, DM-015 activation parsing, and the v2 PreToolUse matcher/raw-denial behavior specified by FR-238..FR-241. These are normative future surfaces, not implementation delivered by Revision 7.\\n   122\\t- Additive phase-3/4 v2 reason-code and hook-vector artifacts in the exact DM-016 inventory. Every v1 artifact remains immutable.\\n   123\\t- Revision-9 typed writer, batch recovery, structured binding, ingest, chain-evidence, and archive-rerender contracts; the additive v3 reason-code corpus extends only `forge-cli/2` and preserves every v1/v2 row byte-identically.\\n   124\\t\\n   125\\t### Modified surfaces\\n   270\\tenforces the executable-fence boundary rather than interpreting those prose labels.\\n   271\\t\\n   272\\tThe `reviewer-facing-eval-triggers` region is the sole maintained reviewer-facing trigger path list and contains exactly these ordered rows:\\n   273\\t\\n   274\\t| control | path patterns |\\n   275\\t|---|---|\\n   276\\t| constitution | rules/** |\\n   277\\t| agent-prompt-template | agents/**, system/codex/prompts/**, .claude/agents/** |\\n   278\\t| reviewer-routing | system/codex/agents/**, system/codex/config.toml, .codex/agents/**, .codex/config.toml, skills/orch