t a verdict; the cap\\nis raised to 60 in the plugin source, commit d637cb2). Plan reviewed: `.refactor/plan-engine.md` as\\nwritten by the split-planner (28 targets), then its revision.\\n\\n## Round 1 — REVISE (2026-09-17)\\n\\nBlocking:\\n\\n- **B1. Quoted `\\\"Engine\\\"` annotations in `_command_lock`.** `_peek_selected_chain` (engine.py:4362),\\n  `_command_run_lock_id` (4383) and the inner `wrapped(self: \\\"Engine\\\", ...)` of\\n  `_serialize_worktree_command` (4515) name `Engine` in string annotations; the inventory records only\\n  `ast.Name` edges, so the plan copied the gap and ruff F821 would fail the wave gate. Fix: the same\\n  `if TYPE_CHECKING: from forge_cli.engine._engine import Engine` guard `_finalize.py` gets, the\\n  \\\"module does not exist yet\\\" type-baseline allowance from wave 2, Risk 5 grep expects two guards.\\n- **B2. Trigger-table window (Risk 7).** After E2 no engine path matches the literal\\n  `scripts/forge/forge_cli/engine.py` in the `reviewer-routing` / `model-provider-version` rows. The\\n  critic asked for the table change to precede E2. Rewritten as Option A (land first on main) and\\n  Option B (accept the window; reintegration verification list). **Operator decision 2026-09-17:\\n  Option B**, on the grounds that Forge is disabled on the branch, no gate evaluates there, and the\\n  reintegration candidate both deletes `engine.py` and carries the repointed tables.\\n- **B3. `plan-engine.json` wave 0 listed `state` and `core` side by side** although `core` references\\n  `state`. Fix: `[state]`, `[core]`, then 17 / 6 / 2 / 1; prose states the orchestrator runs E0, E1,\\n  E2 and the finalize wave by hand.\\n\\nAdvisory (round 1): `_ARCHIVE_MODULE` root re-export reads `None` after the split (nothing reads it;\\nfollow-up bead); E0 accepted and flagged (62 sites, not ~70); E1 accepted and flagged — five fixtures\\npatch `runtime.SCRIPT_DIR`, so a SCRIPT_DIR-based target is not value-identical under tests (confirmed\\nby the E1 gate: `test_cli_merge_adapters` failed; E1 now resolves the shim from `runtime.__file__`);\\nonly `_engine.py` (3,678 lines) is over budget; `external_dependents` in the inventory is empty but all\\n222 moved names are re-exported; nothing beyond E0/E1 departs from a pure move.\\n\\n## Round 2 — APPROVE (2026-09-17)\\n\\nAll three fixes verified mechanically: guard present in the cluster, wave entry and Risk 5; no other\\nquoted annotation exists (`grep -c '\\\"Engine\\\"'` = 3); 28 clusters, 223 symbols assigned once, no\\nintra-wave edge, only backward edge `FinalizeContext -> Engine` (annotation-only); Option B's\\nreintegration list is complete and executable. Advisory: state the exact site count (62 — applied);\\nmake the JSON's scope explicit (the sentence under `## Waves` does); reword \\\"minus the one\\n`TYPE_CHECKING` edge\\\" (applied).\\n\\nUnfinished: the final `__init__.py` code-line count is an estimate (measure in the finalize wave).\\n- Plugin PostToolUse hook (`scripts/forge/invariant-guard.sh`) — advisory invariant feedback after Edit/Write\\n- Plugin Stop/SessionStart hooks — the Stop union of telemetry aggregation plus a drift-staleness nudge, and the SessionStart drift-staleness nudge, in forge-initialized repos\\n- `agents/review-final.md` — instruction-bounded, execution-capable Claude reviewer with a binding verdict; it has no Edit/Write tools but shares the orchestrator's writable worktree, so its no-write boundary is not an OS sandbox\\n- `scripts/forge/{check-halt.sh,acquire-commit-lock.sh,release-commit-lock.sh,run-evals.sh,invariant-guard.sh,configure-dcg.sh,drift-check.sh,drift-staleness.sh,aggregate-telemetry.sh,commit-guard.sh,install.sh}` and `scripts/forge/{check-test-quality.py,archive-run.py,audit-commitments.py,emit-decision-event.py,journal-patterns.py}` — executable governance script surfaces\\n- `scripts/forge/run-scoped-mutation.py` — Python-interpreter-loaded governance helper (the merge path invokes it as `python3 <path>` and the drift path imports it), so it is outside the executable-script inventory\\n- `scripts/forge/forge_cli/` — the Python-interpreter-loaded package the Forge CLI is being split into (bead forge-plugin-95e): `scripts/forge/cli.py` remains the sole invoked entry point and shim that FR-221's matcher and the FR-223 corpora pin; the shim puts its own directory on `sys.path`, re-imports the envelope and policy names by explicit named lists, and forwards attribute reads of every `runtime`, `chain_core`, `engine`, and `app` `__all__` export through a module `__getattr__` (PEP 562), so every historical module attribute stays resolvable while tests reach the package through one shared loader (`tests/_cli_loader.py`); no file under it is executable, and it is outside the executable-script inventory exactly as `run-scoped-mutation.py` is. The package holds `envelope.py` (reason codes, `Refusal`, `FrozenError`, `Outcome`), `policy.py` (the committed-policy parser, whose fence helpers are the canonical patch seams), `runtime.py` (the one canonical module for the patchable controls — the clock, the bounded process runner, the merge lifecycle flag, the Revision-9 state controls, the path roots, the lazily imported coordination modules, the fast-tier mechanical-skip predicate, and the late-bound journal-record builder seam — which every module of the split reads by attribute so one in-memory patch on `forge_cli.runtime` disables a control everywhere), `candidate.py` (the shared bounded, pinned Git-context implementation for immutable tree snapshots, deterministic review evidence, marker identity, and raw produced-commit inspection), the `chain_core/` package (`scripts/forge/forge_cli/chain_core/`, whose root `__init__.py` holds the verbatim `__all__` and re-exports every symbol the historical module defined (its unused imports are not re-bound on the root), and whose modules — the root `__init__.py` and the submodules, together exactly the `scripts/forge/forge_cli/chain_core/` production subjects listed in `.forge/evals/tasks/fr230-phase3-4-v2.manifest.json` — hold the fenced process runner, the FR-235 common-lock arbiter and chain leases, chain and merge-chain storage, merge state and transition validation, the ingest verifiers, and the Revision-9 seam-marker loop (on the package root until bead forge-plugin-4j7 moves it beside `register_coordination_seams`)), `engine.py` (the commit-chain engine, argument-parser construction, finalize pipeline, review/approval/secret-scan helpers, archive surface, merge admission/scope/claim helpers, and Revision-12 bootstrap child protocol; it binds the journal-record builder onto the runtime seam at import), and `app.py` (`MergeEngine`, the shared chain-verb router, argument-parsing and dispatch entry points, and `main`; it obtains the parser and other engine helpers through `forge_cli.engine`). The existing FR-230 phase-3/4 manifest retains its historical production subjects; every changed or added production subject, including `candidate.py`, requires a current applicable Recorded-baseline integrity (`strict-evals`) result binding, plus `fresh-reviewer-evals` when the authenticated-base trigger matches; an unverifiable trigger blocks through its required INVALID path. The split changes no verb, diagnostic, reason code, `--help` byte, or immutable prior corpus.\\n- `scripts/forge/forge_cli/fresh_evals.py` — the non-executable, Python-interpreter-loaded internal collector and verifier for candidate-bound fresh reviewer evaluation; behind the chain-owned `engine.py` launcher adapter it implements authenticated trigger derivation, candidate-tree fixture inventory and oracle withholding, bounded native child execution, canonical request-bound artifacts, manifest verification, and the current-candidate PASS predicate without adding a second CLI entry point\\n- `scripts/forge/cli.py` — the Forge CLI commit-chain slice (FR-210..FR-224): a persisted chain state machine invoked as `python3 \\\"${CLAUDE_PLU